{{also|hiton}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-au-hit on.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|hits on|hitting on|hit on}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[flirt]] with; to [[approach]] and speak to (someone), seeking [[romance]], [[love]], [[sex]], etc.
#: ''That's the third guy that has '''hit on''' her tonight.''
#: ''Guys are '''hitting on''' them almost all the time.''
# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[discover]], [[pinpoint]]; to [[think up]]; to [[realize]].
#: ''He '''hit on''' a great idea for improving the design.''

